\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Tracks areas being explored.\
Fields:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
id\
\
name\
\
status\
\
queries\
\
current_query_index\
\
current_offset\
\
last_searched\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Field descriptions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf0 \strokec2 queries
\f1\fs28 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Stores the Ollama-generated search queries for the niche as JSON.\
Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
[\
  "fishing",\
  "fishing log",\
  "fish tracker",\
  "angler journal",\
  "fishing forecast"\
]\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Queries are generated once and reused until exhausted.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf0 \strokec2 current_query_index
\f1\fs28 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Tracks which query is currently being searched.\
Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
0 = fishing\
1 = fishing log\
2 = fish tracker\
3 = angler journal\
4 = fishing forecast\
\
current_query_index = 2\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The next search will continue with:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
fish tracker\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf0 \strokec2 current_offset
\f0\b0\fs24 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Tracks how far through the results the application has progressed.\
Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
current_offset = 40\
\
Google Play may use dynamically loaded or infinite-scroll search results.\
\
current_offset represents the number of results that have already been\
processed for the current search query.\
\
Do not assume Google Play provides a URL parameter that allows the\
application to jump directly to a specific offset.\
\
Use Playwright to load search results and continue beyond the previously\
processed results. The exact implementation should depend on the current\
behavior of the Google Play website.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Meaning the application has already processed approximately the first 40 results for the current query.\
The next run should continue searching for additional results instead of starting over.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs30\fsmilli15210 \cf0 \strokec2 last_searched
\f0\b0\fs24 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
