\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 Main Loop\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Create a TODO list first. Use the 
\f2\fs26 TODO.md
\f0\fs24  file in the workspace.\
Use this file to keep track of what has and has not been done. Update it as necessary, keep notes, and mark each task as completed when finished.\
The application should run the following loop:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT NICHE\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
GET OR CREATE SEARCH QUERIES\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
SELECT CURRENT QUERY\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
SEARCH GOOGLE PLAY\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
GET NEW RESULTS\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
SKIP APPS ALREADY IN DATABASE\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
SAVE NEW APPS AND METADATA\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
ASK OLLAMA TO EVALUATE EACH NEW APP\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
IF INTERESTING 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f2  SAVE AS OPPORTUNITY\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
UPDATE SEARCH PROGRESS\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f2 \
EXIT
\f0\fs24 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 Selecting a Niche\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Choose a niche that is not exhausted.\
Prefer niches that have been explored the least recently.\
Do not constantly return to the same niche.\
Use:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT *\
FROM niches\
WHERE status = 'ACTIVE'\
ORDER BY\
    CASE WHEN last_searched IS NULL THEN 0 ELSE 1 END,\
    last_searched ASC\
LIMIT 1;\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 \
After processing the niche, update:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
last_searched\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Niches can continue to be added by the user.\
New niches should automatically be included in future searches.\
Keep this simple.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 Searching Google Play\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use Playwright to search the public Google Play website.\
Example search:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
https://play.google.com/store/search?q=fishing&c=apps\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Extract apps from the search results.\
For each new app, collect as much of the following publicly available information as possible:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
Name\
\
Developer\
\
Package Name\
\
URL\
\
Description\
\
Category\
\
Rating\
\
Review Count\
\
Install Count\
\
Last Updated\
\
Price\
\
Contains Ads\
\
Offers In-App Purchases\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 \
Some information may not be available directly from the search results.\
The application may:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Find the app through Google Play search.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Open the individual app page.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Extract the available metadata.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 If package name is unavailable, derive or extract it from the app URL when possible.\
Use conservative request rates.\
Do not bypass CAPTCHAs, access controls, or anti-bot protections.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 Avoid Repeatedly Searching the Same Apps\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is important.\
The program should not always examine only the first results.\
For each niche, generate several related search terms.\
Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
Fishing\
\
fishing\
\
fishing log\
\
fish tracker\
\
angler journal\
\
fishing forecast\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Search queries should be generated once and stored in:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
niches.queries\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The application tracks:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
current_query_index\
\
current_offset\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
Fishing\
\
Current Query:\
fish tracker\
\
Current Offset:\
40\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The next time the application runs, it should continue beyond the first 40 results.\
It should not restart from the beginning.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 Query Generation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Use Ollama to generate a user-defined number of search terms for the niche.\
Example prompt:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
Generate [USER DEFINED NUMBER] different Google Play Store search queries for finding Android apps related to this niche:\
\
FISHING\
\
Return only a JSON array of search queries.\
\
The queries should explore different types of apps within the niche.\
\
Avoid repeating the exact same concept.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Example result:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
[\
  "fishing log",\
  "fish tracker",\
  "angler journal",\
  "fishing forecast",\
  "catch tracker"\
]\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Do not generate new queries every time.\
Generate the queries once.\
Store them in:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
niches.queries\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The application should work through the queries sequentially.\
When one query is exhausted:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
current_query_index += 1\
\
current_offset = 0\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 Exhausting a Search Query\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 A search query is exhausted when:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 It reaches the configured result limit.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Google Play no longer returns additional results.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Or the application repeatedly finds no new apps.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 When a query is exhausted:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
current_query_index += 1\
\
current_offset = 0\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The application then moves to the next query.\
